-- title:
--   Unimodularity of GL₂(K_∞): Haar measures are right invariant
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a number field (a field with a `NumberField` structure), and let $K_\infty =$ `InfiniteAdeleRing K` be its ring of infinite adeles, so that $GL(\mathrm{Fin}\,2, K_\infty)$ denotes the group of units of $2\times 2$ matrices over $K_\infty$, equipped with the measurable space [`AutomorphicForm.glBorelOf (InfiniteAdeleRing K)`](def/AutomorphicForm_TwistedOrbital.html#L57), which by definition is the Borel $\sigma$-algebra `borel _` generated by the topology of this group. Let $\nu$ be a measure on $GL(\mathrm{Fin}\,2, K_\infty)$ for that Borel $\sigma$-algebra, and assume $\nu$ is a Haar measure in the sense of `Measure.IsHaarMeasure` with respect to this same $\sigma$-algebra, i.e. it is left invariant, finite on compact sets, positive on nonempty open sets and regular. The conclusion is that $\nu$ is also right invariant: for every $x \in GL(\mathrm{Fin}\,2, K_\infty)$ the pushforward of $\nu$ along right multiplication by $x$ is again $\nu$. Thus $GL_2(K_\infty)$ is unimodular, the assertion being made for an arbitrary Haar measure rather than for a single normalised one.
--
--   This is the unimodularity of $GL_2$ over the product of the archimedean completions of a number field, stated in the form that left invariance of a Haar measure on $GL(\mathrm{Fin}\,2, K_\infty)$ forces right invariance. It is used in the measure-theoretic groundwork for orbital and twisted orbital integrals on $GL_2$ of the adeles, where archimedean and finite places are compared through the restricted-product factorisation of an adelic Haar measure; the proof cites the factorisation theorem [`AutomorphicForm.exists_integral_eq_mul_integral_mul_prod_integral_localHaar_of_isHaarMeasure`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.exists_integral_eq_mul_integral_mul_prod_integral_localHaar_of_isHaarMeasure), the right invariance of the adelic Haar measure [`NumberField.AdelicHaar.isMulRightInvariant_adelicGLHaar`](thm.html#NumberField.AdelicHaar.isMulRightInvariant_adelicGLHaar), and second countability of $GL_2$ of the adeles.
